  triage:title "Near-identical AckRequest-to-into_write_request() construction duplicated across atm-daemon test modules" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/https_transport.rs (~line 1085-1095) and crates/atm-daemon/src/local_tcp_transport.rs (~line 712-723) both hand-construct the same AckRequest { home_dir, current_dir, caller_identity, caller_chat_id: None, caller_team, message_id, reply_body }.into_write_request() shape. Both are in the atm-daemon crate and could share a helper in crates/atm-daemon/src/test_support.rs (e.g. sample_ack_write_request(message_id) -> WriteRequest), which currently has no public helpers. A third occurrence in crates/atm-core/src/api.rs is in a separate crate so cross-crate sharing isn't practical there." ;
